  "body": [
    {
      "_key": "en",
      "_type": "object",
      "value": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000001",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000000",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Places To Go In Rosetta {Rasheed}"
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "h2"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000009",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000002",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "In Rosetta, also known as Rasheed, a walk down its streets unfolds a treasure trove of architectural wonders, each telling a story from a bygone era. This town, rich in "
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000004",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "000000000003"
              ],
              "text": "Ottoman-era"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000005",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " architecture, offers an insightful glimpse into "
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000007",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "000000000006"
              ],
              "text": "Egypt’s"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000008",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " diverse historical layers."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000003",
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ottoman_Empire#:~:text=The%20Ottoman%20Empire%2C%20historically%20and,16th%20and%20early%2018th%20centuries.",
              "newTab": true
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000006",
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "http://travel2egypt.org/about-egypt/",
              "newTab": false
            }
          ],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "00000000000b",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000000a",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Ottoman Houses: A Glimpse into the Past"
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "h3"
        },
        {
          "_key": "00000000000d",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000000c",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Rosetta’s Ottoman houses, fashioned in the traditional Delta style with small, flat bricks painted in alternating shades of red and black, are a visual delight. These three-story structures often feature an upper floor that slightly overhangs the lower, reminiscent of an ornate, upside-down chocolate wedding cake. The houses are adorned with mashrabiyyas, the intricate wooden screens serving as windows, adding to their distinctive charm."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "00000000000f",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000000e",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "House of Mizouni: An Interior Marvel "
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "h3"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000011",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000010",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Among these architectural gems, the House of Mizouni, dating back to 1740, stands out for its exquisite interior. Rising five stories, it features similar designs across the main floors, with living and reception rooms facing north and smaller rooms encircling a courtyard. The highlight is the rooftop terrace, enclosed by high walls that offer a secluded vantage point over the town."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000013",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000012",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "House of Amasyali: A Facade of Elegance"
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "h3"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000015",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000014",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "The House of Amasyali boasts Rosetta’s finest exterior, with vibrant colors and intricate details. Although currently closed to visitors, its reopening promises a showcase of splendid wooden ceilings and wall decorations, including extensive use of mother-of-pearl in the mashrabiyyas."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000017",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000016",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Mill of Abu Shahin: A Functional Relic"
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "h3"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000019",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000018",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Adjacent to the House of Amasyali is the Mill of Abu Shahin, a beautifully restored, fully functional mill open to visitors. Here, guests can interact with the mill’s mechanics, offering a hands-on historical experience."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "00000000001b",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000001a",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "The Quarter of Ramadan House"
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "h3"
        },
        {
          "_key": "00000000001d",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000001c",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "The Ramadan House and its surrounding six houses are prime examples of well-restored exteriors, each featuring unique variations of the common Ottoman style. The Ramadan House, though still under restoration, contains a room with a ceiling that’s a hidden artistic marvel."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "00000000001f",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000001e",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Thabet House: The Oldest of its Kind"
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "h3"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000021",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000020",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Dating back to 1709, the Thabet House is renowned for being the oldest Ottoman merchant’s house in Rosetta. Its distinctive slanting corners leading up to traditionally squared-off roof corners set it apart from its contemporaries."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000023",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000022",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Al-Mahali Mosque: A Unique Architectural Ensemble"
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "h3"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000025",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000024",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Al-Mahali Mosque, with its 99 unique columns representing the 99 names of God in Islam, is an intriguing site. The columns, sourced from various religious buildings, symbolize the continuity of faith and tradition."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000027",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000026",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Muallaqa Mosque: Hidden Grandeur"
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "h3"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000029",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000028",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Tucked between narrow streets, the Muallaqa Mosque is notable for its rare first-floor balustrade. Its interior, more grandiose than its modest exterior suggests, offers a surprising contrast."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "00000000002a",
          "_pendingImage": "https://travel2egypt.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/02/IMG_5890-1024x683-1.jpg",
          "_type": "image",
          "alt": [
            {
              "_key": "en",
              "value": "場所"
            }
          ],
          "caption": [
            {
              "_key": "en",
              "value": "The quiet beauty of Rosetta's riverbank, where boats dock and history stands tall"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_key": "00000000002b",
          "_pendingImage": "https://travel2egypt.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/02/Rosetta-Egypt.jpg",
          "_type": "image",
          "alt": [
            {
              "_key": "en",
